# Install Obot Sentry on macOS

Manually install `obot-sentry` to run one-off scans or install hooks
yourself.

1. Open Terminal and install the binary:

   ```sh
   sudo install -m 755 obot-sentry /usr/local/bin/obot-sentry
   ```

2. Configure Obot Sentry by writing the same preferences domain an MDM
   profile delivers, replacing `REPLACE_WITH_ENROLLMENT_KEY` with your
   enrollment key:

   ```sh
   sudo defaults write /Library/Preferences/com.obot.obot-sentry ServerURL -string "{{.serverURL}}"
   sudo defaults write /Library/Preferences/com.obot.obot-sentry EnrollmentKey -string "REPLACE_WITH_ENROLLMENT_KEY"
   sudo defaults write /Library/Preferences/com.obot.obot-sentry ScanIntervalMinutes -string "{{.scanIntervalMinutes}}"
   ```

## Run a scan

```sh
obot-sentry scan --submit
```

By default, scans are submitted at most once every {{.scanIntervalMinutes}} minutes; runs within that window skip submission.

## Install hooks

```sh
sudo obot-sentry hook-install
```

## Uninstall

Remove the binary, the configuration, and the device identity and scan
state:

```sh
sudo rm -f /usr/local/bin/obot-sentry
sudo defaults delete /Library/Preferences/com.obot.obot-sentry
sudo rm -rf "/Library/Application Support/obot/obot-sentry"
rm -rf "$HOME/Library/Application Support/obot/obot-sentry" "$HOME/Library/Caches/obot/obot-sentry"
```
